<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lament for Ur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 2000 BCE, around the fall of Ur</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century-bce">21st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lament for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur">Ur</a>, or Lamentation over the city of Ur, is a Sumerian lament composed around the time when Ur fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamites">Elamites</a> and its Third Dynasty came to an end, about 2000 BC. The dynasty had ruled for around a hundred years. Invading Elamites raided the temple treasury, the centre of power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumer">Sumer</a> moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isin">Isin</a>, and control of Ur's trade passed to several leading families of the city.</p></div>
